WEBVTT

00:00:00.670 --> 00:00:02.680
You don't understand.

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:05.550
Those who turn against the elites 
will always be crushed.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:07.340
Pendulum Summon!

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.880
Come out, my monsters!

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:16.540
Continuous Trap Fraud Freeze!

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:20.350
This card activates when you Special 
Summon a monster from your hand,

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:22.280
and returns that monster to your hand.

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:23.200
What?

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.480
My god!

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:29.630
The big Pendulum Summon he managed 
was treated as a fraud!

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:34.080
As long as he has that trap card, Pendulum Summoning 
will be treated as fraudulent?

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.600
And Tokumatsu has Lightshower on the field.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:40.820
Each time Yuya draws, it deals 1500 damage to him.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:42.550
Yuya...

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:48.580
D-Wheels.

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:52.840
Riding duels are fought while 
racing on these machines,

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:54.490
which are an evolution of the duel disks.

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:57.930
They combine speed and thrills for the ultimate show,

00:00:57.930 --> 00:01:00.120
a symbol of freedom to all.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:37.900
The Man Who Abandoned the Draw

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:40.590
What a pity.

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:44.110
I've sealed your special technique, 
the Pendulum Summon.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:48.860
You now have neither opportunity 
nor time to oppose me!

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:51.690
You've changed.

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:55.790
This isn't the way that Enjoy Chojiro duels.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:57.520
Enjoy Chojiro?

00:02:57.520 --> 00:02:58.990
Don't call me that!

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:03.430
Now I'm "Autumn Rain Chojiro."

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:06.730
Because those who duel the boss will lose,

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:10.140
have their cards stolen, and cry a rain of tears.

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:12.940
That's why we started calling him that.

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:15.400
Now, that you have no monsters to shield yourself,

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:19.240
it's only a matter of time before 
you cry a rain of tears, too.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:25.480
I summon a monster from my hand 
in facedown defense position.

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:32.010
It's true that Fraud Freeze's effect

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:34.620
only affects monsters that are Special Summoned.

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:37.030
You can still Normal Summon.

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:39.130
Now, I end my turn.

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:43.840
If you don't want to be drenched by the rain 
of tears, you should prepare an umbrella.

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:45.810
My turn!

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:49.170
If I draw now, then Lightshower loses its ability

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:53.510
to deal you 1500 damage whenever you draw.

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:57.250
But I use Lightshower's effect to skip my draw!

00:03:58.490 --> 00:04:03.150
Next turn, when you draw, you'll take 1500 damage

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:05.820
and tumble down the path to self-destruction.

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:07.120
Nice one, boss!

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:09.240
Your victory combo is locked in!

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:10.460
What are you talking about?!

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:13.160
I don't need your cheers.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:16.110
I don't need anyone's cheers,

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:18.450
as long as I win the duel.

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:22.140
That's enough to prove that I'm a powerful elite.

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:24.040
What a weirdo...

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:28.200
Duels are all about the cheers 
that prove you've stood out.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.980
That only goes for you.

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:33.550
My sure-kill combo is now complete.

00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:38.550
If you surrender now, I'll let you off 
with just half of your cards.

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:42.830
All you've done is secure your 
combo, not your victory.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:44.560
I still have a chance!

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:49.030
In the face of overwhelming power, 
it's impossible to change anything!

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:51.900
As long as I don't give up, I know I can change it!

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:55.660
I see I have no choice but to force the truth on you.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:56.570
Battle!

00:04:56.570 --> 00:04:58.710
I attack with Lightshower!

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:04.680
I now end my turn.

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:07.660
My turn...

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:11.400
My life is 2500.

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:14.600
This draw will make me take 1500 damage.

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:16.300
So this is my final draw.

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:23.800
Lightshower's effect

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:27.910
deals 1500 damage to you whenever you draw!

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:37.420
That's bad! At this rate, Yuya will destroy himself!

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:42.150
I summon a monster in facedown defense position.

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:46.860
I now end my turn.

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:49.330
Is that the end?

00:05:50.210 --> 00:05:51.300
It's over.

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:52.860
My turn.

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:55.690
I use Lightshower's effect to skip my draw.

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:58.740
Lightshower attacks your defense-position monster.

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:05.180
It's just like last turn. At this rate...

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:08.430
On your next turn, when you draw,

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:11.210
you will reduce your own life points to 0.

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:14.150
Then the match will be over.

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:18.090
I end my turn.

00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:19.960
Now, it's your turn.

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:23.360
Go ahead. Take a card.

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:25.330
Your draw of failure.

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:27.960
He's changed so much.

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:30.540
Yeah, he's nothing like he used to be.

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:33.300
What's this "Enjoy" thing you've been talking about?

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:35.270
"Enjoy Chojiro."

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:40.010
Back when we were still kids, he was 
a duelist we all really admired.

00:06:40.010 --> 00:06:42.250
Admired? Him?

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:45.950
Yeah, he was the Commons' star of hope.

00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:48.540
He wasn't obsessed with winning or losing.

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:50.360
He just wanted to enjoy the duel.

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:52.590
Enjoy!

00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:57.330
With his first draw, he'd always make 
a miracle happen and win.

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:00.000
Even after he became a popular duelist,

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.300
he would come to teach dueling 
to Commons children.

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:08.940
Draw! Draw!

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:08.340
I often attended his duel classes.

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:10.470
You punk!

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:11.610
And any time he saw young people fighting...

00:07:12.050 --> 00:07:14.950
Stop this foolish bickering.

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:18.080
If you have the energy to cause 
trouble, have a duel instead.

00:07:19.930 --> 00:07:24.970
A duel isn't just a way of fighting. It's a way 
to learn about your opponent and yourself.

00:07:24.970 --> 00:07:27.660
It will build bonds between you.

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:29.230
That is what dueling is about.

00:07:33.670 --> 00:07:37.640
Chojiro! Chojiro! Chojiro!

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:40.340
Enjoy!

00:07:40.340 --> 00:07:42.400
But what about now?

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:45.400
He just crushes all the cards 
his opponent tries to play,

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:46.990
and waits for them to self-destruct.

00:07:46.990 --> 00:07:51.720
If he was such a success, what's he doing in prison?

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:52.820
I don't know...

00:07:53.350 --> 00:07:59.000
He was badly beaten by Tops 
duelists and lost his way.

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:01.290
I heard he'd fallen hard, but...

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:06.270
What's wrong? You understand there's 
nothing left you can do, don't you?

00:08:06.270 --> 00:08:10.540
Give up! This match doesn't end 
except with your loss!

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:13.560
Nothing's been decided yet!

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:18.340
We don't know what will happen. 
That's what makes it fun!

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:21.910
Shut up! There's no point in enjoying a duel!

00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:22.840
There is!

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:25.850
You can make everyone smile...

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:30.080
I learned that from my mother and father.

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:32.590
From all the duelists I've fought up till now!

00:08:32.590 --> 00:08:33.830
Shut up!

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:35.790
It won't change anything.

00:08:36.380 --> 00:08:40.350
No matter how you resist, 
there's no changing destiny!

00:08:40.350 --> 00:08:42.900
It's all pointless!

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:47.640
Everyone's equal up there, but it's still 
Tops above and Commons below.

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:50.680
And the difference between is enormous!

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:53.530
I broke down that wall with my dueling!

00:08:54.110 --> 00:08:57.630
In a duel, there are no Tops or Commons. 
I thought I could change it!

00:08:57.630 --> 00:09:02.990
Thinking that, I challenged the Tops duelists. But...

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:09.630
I ended up facing a firing squad of those

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:13.300
who'd used their money to buy strong cards!

00:09:13.730 --> 00:09:19.430
The audience's cheers turned to boos, 
and eventually to mockery.

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:23.860
I thought...

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:28.970
If they could turn to boos and mockery 
so easily, I no longer needed cheers.

00:09:28.970 --> 00:09:30.890
I didn't need smiles!

00:09:32.540 --> 00:09:36.690
I was granted a comeback duel. 
It was my last chance.

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:40.840
And in my desperation to avoid a loss at any cost,

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:42.260
I resorted to fraud!

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:45.770
In that moment, I was finished!

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:50.010
Duels can't open up the future. 
They can't change anything!

00:09:50.660 --> 00:09:56.200
Ever since, my duels have been nothing more 
than a tool to survive here, in prison.

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:03.740
Since then, I abandoned my belief in duels 
that depend on the luck of the draw.

00:10:04.130 --> 00:10:07.050
And from there, I worked out this sure-win combo.

00:10:07.610 --> 00:10:13.390
The power I've built up for ten years, after 
learning that nothing ever changes...

00:10:13.990 --> 00:10:16.130
You can't possibly change that!

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:20.370
We're going to see whether or not I can change it!

00:10:26.740 --> 00:10:28.090
Draw!

00:10:31.780 --> 00:10:33.480
Now, it's over!

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:38.120
Lightshower's effect deals 1500 damage to you.

00:10:40.180 --> 00:10:43.150
The card I drew is Performapal Rain Goat!

00:10:43.650 --> 00:10:47.630
I can send this card to the graveyard, 
to negate effect damage!

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:50.030
Yeah!

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:54.000
A true raincoat, for shelter from the rain of tears.

00:10:55.160 --> 00:10:57.470
A mere stopgap measure.

00:10:57.740 --> 00:11:02.070
It isn't! When a Performapal is sent 
from my hand to the graveyard,

00:11:02.330 --> 00:11:06.540
I can Special Summon Teeter Totter 
Hopper in defense position!

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:08.570
That card...

00:11:08.570 --> 00:11:10.450
The one that was destroyed last turn...

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:15.590
Once per turn, when this card is Special Summoned, 
it can't be destroyed by battle.

00:11:15.930 --> 00:11:20.810
Then, during the End Phase of your turn, 
I can send this card to the graveyard,

00:11:20.810 --> 00:11:25.560
to add one Performapal, Level 3 or below, 
from my graveyard to my hand!

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:26.460
What?

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:30.870
Right now, he has Performapal 
Rain Goat in his graveyard.

00:11:31.190 --> 00:11:33.130
On Tokumatsu's next turn,

00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:37.800
he can send Teeter Totter Hopper, which can't 
be destroyed by battle, to the graveyard,

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:39.940
add Rain Goat to his hand,

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:47.150
and then negate Lightshower's effect by 
sending Rain Goat to the graveyard,

00:11:47.150 --> 00:11:50.040
while again Special Summoning Teeter Totter Hopper.

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:53.620
I see... It's an unbeatable infinite loop.

00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:56.380
A sure-kill combo against an infinite loop.

00:11:56.380 --> 00:11:57.830
Not bad, Yuya!

00:11:58.120 --> 00:11:59.440
H-He...

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:02.030
He deflected the boss's sure-kill combo.

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:04.010
I changed how things were going.

00:12:05.970 --> 00:12:07.930
Impudent child...

00:12:14.510 --> 00:12:18.330
Hey, Mr. Jailer! How about this?

00:12:18.330 --> 00:12:19.470
Pipe down.

00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:22.480
I'm so curious about Mr. Tokumatsu's 
duel, I can't help myself.

00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:23.900
Take this, and let me go!

00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:25.160
Mine, too, please!

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:26.710
Mine, too!

00:12:26.710 --> 00:12:29.490
And mine! Please!

00:12:32.930 --> 00:12:34.270
Here, they are!

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:35.530
Mr. Tokumatsu, I've been waiting for this!

00:12:35.530 --> 00:12:36.890
This is great!

00:12:36.890 --> 00:12:38.040
We made it in time!

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:40.140
The boss is pretty popular, huh?

00:12:40.140 --> 00:12:44.330
But that unbeatable infinite loop is trouble.

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:47.250
The boss won't draw because 
of Lightshower's effect.

00:12:47.550 --> 00:12:49.180
But what about him?

00:12:49.180 --> 00:12:52.480
Eventually, he'll run out of cards and have to forfeit.

00:12:52.480 --> 00:12:53.950
Are you stupid?

00:12:53.950 --> 00:12:56.090
In the meantime, how many draws will he get?

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:58.520
Now, I end my turn!

00:12:58.520 --> 00:13:03.440
I've got plenty of time before I run out of 
cards, and we have a big audience.

00:13:03.440 --> 00:13:04.700
So let's have fun together!

00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:07.680
You think I'll give you that time?!

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:09.430
I'll crush you first.

00:13:12.340 --> 00:13:13.940
My turn.

00:13:13.940 --> 00:13:14.940
Th-The boss is gonna...

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:15.910
...draw?!

00:13:16.200 --> 00:13:18.610
He isn't using Lightshower's effect?

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:21.080
Go! Yeah!

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:26.390
How many years has it been

00:13:26.930 --> 00:13:31.020
since I staked my fate on this two-finger draw?

00:13:33.220 --> 00:13:35.290
Did the boss just smile?

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:37.920
Since the day I performed that fraudulent draw,

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:41.820
no matter how many times I tried, 
I've never drawn that card...

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:45.080
It was as if the card abandoned me.

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:49.290
Chojiro! Chojiro! Chojiro!

00:13:49.290 --> 00:13:53.740
Chojiro! Chojiro! Chojiro!

00:13:53.740 --> 00:13:56.810
Chojiro! Chojiro!

00:13:56.810 --> 00:14:01.240
Chojiro! Chojiro! Chojiro!

00:13:57.710 --> 00:14:00.270
Okay, everyone! That's the way!

00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:01.720
Let's make some noise!

00:14:03.420 --> 00:14:05.760
Chojiro! Chojiro!

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:10.460
That little brat's made them this happy, has he?

00:14:13.720 --> 00:14:15.260
You idiots!

00:14:15.260 --> 00:14:18.770
Look at you, with light sparkling in your eyes!

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:22.510
No, it isn't just them...

00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:25.480
Enjoy!

00:14:25.480 --> 00:14:27.450
It gives me shivers!

00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:32.080
Here it comes! I activate my 
spell card Super Koi Koi!

00:14:32.080 --> 00:14:32.950
There it is!

00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:34.420
The miracle draw!

00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:37.890
This card's effect lets me draw three cards

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:41.360
and Special Summon any Flower 
Cardians among them.

00:14:41.700 --> 00:14:44.940
But any non-Cardians are sent to my graveyard,

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:47.800
dealing 1000 points of damage to me for each.

00:14:49.270 --> 00:14:50.560
Here I go...

00:14:50.560 --> 00:14:52.570
The draw on which my destiny rests.

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:54.670
There, he is! The best ever!

00:14:54.670 --> 00:14:57.240
Duels are akin to life.

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:01.050
You only live once.

00:15:01.050 --> 00:15:03.410
You win sometimes, and you lose sometimes.

00:15:03.410 --> 00:15:06.860
Don't be ashamed of defeat. 
Don't be complacent in victory.

00:15:06.860 --> 00:15:09.550
In other words, let's enjoy!

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:11.610
Enjoy!

00:15:11.610 --> 00:15:13.020
Enjoy!

00:15:14.950 --> 00:15:16.930
For starters, the first card!

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:19.020
Come on, come on! Come on, come on!

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:20.900
Come on, come on, come on, come on!

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:23.130
Enjoy!

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:25.900
Flower Cardian Clover with Boar!

00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:29.140
The second card...

00:15:29.140 --> 00:15:31.870
Come on, come on! Come on, 
come on, come on!

00:15:31.870 --> 00:15:33.610
Enjoy!

00:15:34.130 --> 00:15:36.810
Flower Cardian Maple with Deer!

00:15:36.810 --> 00:15:39.120
And the third card!

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:42.320
Come on, come on! Come on, come on! Come on!

00:15:42.320 --> 00:15:44.560
Enjoy!

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:47.760
Flower Cardian Peony with Butterfly!

00:15:48.790 --> 00:15:50.410
All three are Flower Cardians!

00:15:50.410 --> 00:15:52.750
That's the Enjoy Chojiro I know!

00:15:52.750 --> 00:15:55.880
Well? My draws haven't grown any weaker.

00:15:55.880 --> 00:16:01.210
And the attack and defense points of all monsters 
Special Summoned with Super Koi Koi

00:16:01.210 --> 00:16:04.180
become 0, and their levels become 2.

00:16:04.490 --> 00:16:10.650
Level 2 Peony with Butterfly tunes Clover 
with Boar and Maple with Deer!

00:16:14.580 --> 00:16:19.870
The courage of the boar, the elegance of the deer,

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:22.730
the beauty of the butterfly!

00:16:23.810 --> 00:16:25.700
Synchro Summon!

00:16:26.510 --> 00:16:30.730
Level 6 Flower Cardian Boardefly!

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:34.410
Battle!

00:16:35.110 --> 00:16:38.110
Lightshower, attack Teeter Totter Hopper!

00:16:38.550 --> 00:16:42.850
Once per turn, Teeter Totter Hopper's 
effect keeps it from being destroyed.

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:45.600
But it only works once.

00:16:46.050 --> 00:16:49.020
Boardefly attacks Teeter Totter Hopper, as well,

00:16:49.420 --> 00:16:54.580
dealing piercing damage against 
defense-position monsters!

00:16:57.430 --> 00:16:58.400
Yuya!

00:16:58.400 --> 00:17:00.580
Now, I end my turn.

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:04.520
You have 200 life points remaining. You can't win.

00:17:04.520 --> 00:17:07.850
But it isn't over yet, is it?

00:17:07.850 --> 00:17:08.610
Of course not!

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:12.710
The fun is only getting started!

00:17:13.220 --> 00:17:15.770
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:17:15.770 --> 00:17:18.300
The entertainment duel is about to begin!

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:21.690
Can I recover from this danger 
and turn things around?

00:17:21.690 --> 00:17:23.390
Just you wait and see!

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:28.220
My turn!

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:30.960
I got it!

00:17:31.410 --> 00:17:34.100
Spell card Pendulum Storm.

00:17:34.100 --> 00:17:38.660
To activate this card, I destroy all 
cards in my Pendulum Zones.

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:41.470
He won't use Pendulum?

00:17:41.770 --> 00:17:46.860
Don't worry. When one curtain 
lowers, another one rises.

00:17:46.860 --> 00:17:48.450
That's what entertainment dueling is!

00:17:50.760 --> 00:17:53.360
First, let's use Pendulum Storm's effect

00:17:53.360 --> 00:17:57.150
to destroy one spell or trap card 
on your side of the field.

00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:01.800
He destroyed Fraud Freeze!

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:04.830
There goes that wretched curse, right?

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:08.200
I set the Pendulum Scale with Scale 2 
Performapal Sellshell Crab

00:18:08.200 --> 00:18:13.060
and Scale 4 Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:27.220
Now, I can summon multiple Level 3 
monsters simultaneously.

00:18:27.220 --> 00:18:28.950
Yes... Time to strike back!

00:18:29.260 --> 00:18:39.600
Pendulum! Pendulum! Pendulum!

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:42.570
Swing, my soul's pendulum.

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:45.540
Draw an arc of light in the sky!

00:18:45.880 --> 00:18:47.340
Pendulum Summon!

00:18:47.340 --> 00:18:49.930
Come out, my monsters!

00:18:51.920 --> 00:18:55.210
From my Extra Deck, Performapal Bit Bite Turtle!

00:18:55.500 --> 00:18:57.920
And Timegazer Magician, too!

00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:02.320
Battle! Bit Bite Turtle attacks Lightshower!

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:04.160
Have you lost your mind?

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:07.690
Attacking Lightshower, who has 3000 attack 
points, with an 800-point monster?

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:12.360
Now, here's a surprising trick.

00:19:12.700 --> 00:19:15.100
This is Bit Bite Turtle's effect...

00:19:15.680 --> 00:19:18.840
The monster that destroys Bit Bite 
Turtle is, itself, destroyed!

00:19:19.640 --> 00:19:22.210
But you still lose, due to the damage you took.

00:19:22.840 --> 00:19:25.180
Odd-Eyes's Pendulum Effect activates!

00:19:25.440 --> 00:19:31.030
Once per turn, I can negate battle damage 
dealt to a Pendulum Monster!

00:19:31.880 --> 00:19:35.220
Oh, is that it? Not bad at all...

00:19:35.530 --> 00:19:38.860
Now, Sellshell Crab's effect activates!

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:42.570
When a Pendulum Monster on my 
side of the field is destroyed,

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:45.930
I can Special Summon a monster 
to the Pendulum Zone.

00:19:46.190 --> 00:19:48.630
Come out, Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:19:52.340 --> 00:19:53.300
Battle!

00:19:53.660 --> 00:19:56.540
I attack Boardefly with Odd-Eyes!

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:59.280
I activate my trap card Fraud Check.

00:19:59.550 --> 00:20:02.800
On this turn, Cardians cannot 
be destroyed by battle!

00:20:04.920 --> 00:20:05.630
He dodged it!

00:20:05.630 --> 00:20:07.220
But the damage goes through!

00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:09.420
Odd-Eyes's effect activates!

00:20:09.740 --> 00:20:14.440
When battling a monster, Level 5 or 
above, battle damage is doubled!

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:16.190
Reaction Force!

00:20:19.560 --> 00:20:23.530
And I activate my Quick-Play 
Spell Pendulum Climax!

00:20:25.310 --> 00:20:28.110
I tribute a Pendulum Monster on my side of the field,

00:20:28.110 --> 00:20:32.710
to equip a monster of the same level, 
on your field, to a monster it fought.

00:20:33.050 --> 00:20:36.020
I equip Flower Cardian Cherry Blossom 
with Curtain to Odd-Eyes!

00:20:36.660 --> 00:20:40.950
It increases its attack points by those of 
Cherry Blossom with Curtain halved!

00:20:40.950 --> 00:20:43.190
3500 attack points, eh?

00:20:43.190 --> 00:20:45.520
And now, for the finale!

00:20:45.520 --> 00:20:49.430
With this effect, Odd-Eyes can attack again!

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:52.900
Well, let's battle.

00:20:52.900 --> 00:20:55.370
Odd-Eyes, attack Boardefly.

00:20:55.700 --> 00:20:58.070
Spiral Strike Burst!

00:21:02.210 --> 00:21:04.810
And Reaction Force's effect 
doubles the damage dealt.

00:21:15.560 --> 00:21:16.430
Boss...

00:21:16.430 --> 00:21:17.420
Boss!

00:21:18.850 --> 00:21:19.820
I lost.

00:21:19.820 --> 00:21:21.380
B-Boss...

00:21:25.600 --> 00:21:27.210
That was fun.

00:21:27.210 --> 00:21:29.040
I haven't fought a duel like this in a while.

00:21:29.040 --> 00:21:30.810
Chojiro!

00:21:31.990 --> 00:21:48.490
Chojiro! Chojiro! Chojiro!

00:21:48.750 --> 00:21:50.950
Enjoy!

00:21:51.120 --> 00:21:53.900
Enjoy!

00:21:55.700 --> 00:21:57.630
How is she doing?

00:21:58.150 --> 00:22:02.600
She caused a lot of trouble at first, but she 
seems to have calmed down.

00:22:03.300 --> 00:22:08.710
I see... Then, let us go and visit her.

00:23:45.840 --> 00:23:48.240
Crow... Wait, Crow!

00:23:48.240 --> 00:23:49.670
Did Shinji tell you?

00:23:50.420 --> 00:23:51.850
About the duel tournament?

00:23:51.850 --> 00:23:57.500
You should go and enjoy it. 
And starting today, we aren't allies!

00:23:57.500 --> 00:23:59.050
Why not?

00:23:59.050 --> 00:24:03.040
I owe Shinji a favor. I'll work with him.

00:24:03.040 --> 00:24:05.580
Crow... Don't tell me...

00:24:06.630 --> 00:24:11.170
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
The Great Entertainment Duel Tournament!!

00:24:11.170 --> 00:24:13.260
The fun's only getting started!
